<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka ends firmer, retains early edge.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka ends firmer, retains early edge.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-05-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka retained its early edge to close firmer at 43.7490/7510 to the dollar in interbank trading on Sunday compared with a previous close at 43.7500/7600, dealers said.</p>
<p>Taka opened at 43.7490/7550 per dollar and edged up further by midday on an easing of U.S. dollar supply.</p>
<p>The call money was traded at seven to nine percent against a previous eight to 11 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
